   "text": "The model inspected `api.py` and saw that `_query` always used POST [T0B16:<RANGE>self.response = self.session.post(</RANGE>]. It then typed in a `_query_public` GET helper and a `query_public` method using a python heredoc [T0B19:<RANGE>self.response = self.session.get(</RANGE>]. A mocked check showed the correct calls [T0B22:<RANGE>call('https://api.kraken.com/0/public/Depth', params={'pair': 'XXBTZUSD', 'count': '10'}, timeout=5)</RANGE>]. The fix itself is the model's own work, and the metadata shows a passing reward [R0M.trace_lab].\n\nThe ending went wrong:\n- The model gave plain-text completion summaries, which the harness rejected [T0B26:<RANGE>ERROR: Missing required fields: analysis, plan, commands</RANGE>].\n- It then invoked mark_task_complete [T0B29:<RANGE>mark_task_complete()</RANGE>].\n- When asked to confirm [T0B30:<RANGE>If so, include \"task_complete\": true in your JSON response again.</RANGE>], it sent echo commands instead [T0B31:<RANGE>echo confirmed</RANGE>].\n- It kept doing this, ignoring a harness nudge [T0B72:<RANGE>you are repeating; change approach or finish</RANGE>], until the run was cut off with LoopBreakStop after 51 episodes [R0M.trace_lab].\n\nThe handshake never completed, so the stop reason is 'other'. The run was not a clean ending, even though the graded code passes.",
